wd=./step1_historical49_extractreads_from_metagenome
for h49, with 49 raw genomes (10 lopez r1 r2, 31 PL r1 r2, and 8 HB collapsed fastq), we map to At and map to Ps with HTF and TFA haplotypes. (the new three PL0105, PL0087 and HB0808)

from the very raw fastq for h49 samples that after dedup has above 60% cov prop to ATUE5 ref (exclude HTF and TFA haplotypes).

1. we did two strategies to run from fastq to bam (for HB_PL do collapse then map, and for lopez, do collapse + r1 and r2 truncated map, then combine).

2. Then we calculate endogenous prop (At number / all, Ps number / all, rest are others), this are before dedup, which means all the reads mapped to one ref no matter dup
 (ps ref exclude haplotypes... in total 5941441 and the reads mapped to 1-37 contigs)

3. Ps bams were derived from unmmaped reads after At mapping (before dedup and q20, seperately from unmapped.collapsed and unmapped.r1r2 then merge).

4. we then calculate cov and depth to the two speices after dedup bams... (lopez use rmdup since the header is messy combined paired and single, others use markdup -r)

The stats summary suppfig1 and metadata supptable1 scripts are in suppfig1AB

5. run mapdamage, run length distribution and insert size for lopez 10, run tree 83+49 after dedup.

6. run HTF assembly with dedup bams, run HTF kmer with dedup h49, and Oantigen with dedup.
